# Corpus scope for `graphify`. Patterns follow gitignore semantics and are also
# matched against any single path segment — so a bare `plugins` drops every path
# containing a `plugins/` segment.
#
# The point of this file: `agents/<squad>/` is a CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, so it holds
# Claude Code's own runtime state (vendored plugin marketplace, session
# transcripts, the upstream changelog) alongside our squad prompts. Without this
# file the corpus is 1603 files / 3.0M words, of which ~93% is that runtime
# state — roughly 60 LLM subagents per full build, for no knowledge at all.
#
# We keep exactly two things out of agents/: `CLAUDE.md` and `agents/*/agents/*.md`
# (the squad and role prompts). Those ARE project knowledge. Do not add a bare
# `agents` pattern here — it would match that path segment and drop them.

# --- Claude Code runtime state (vendored, not ours) ---
plugins
projects
shell-snapshots
statsig
todos
agents/*/cache
agents/*/jobs
agents/*/plans

# --- Telemetry and run artifacts (regenerated, not knowledge) ---
.state
graphify-out

# --- Build output and vendored deps ---
node_modules
ui/dist
.spike-a1
